{"nodes": [{"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_02_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment", "label": "Issue 02: PR Split Reuse and Assignment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/issues/02-pr-split-reuse-and-assignment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved. src/screener/splits.py became the shared split seam: assign_splits owns the cluster-grouped 20% holdout and 5-fold rule and assign_pr_splits accepts an optional primary assignment, reusing it per cluster and assigning PR-only clusters with the same seed and stratification; assignment_source records per-row provenance and the summary records split_source. The test phase fills the global holdout quota across strata so reused primary test clusters cannot drag the holdout away from 20%, and household identity is the (cluster, household) pair because DHS hv002 numbers repeat across clusters. Real PR-only run: 1,808,013 rows, 30,125 clusters, 361,364 test rows (19.99%), leakage checks pass; final validation rejects degenerate partitions and non-covering summaries."}], "edges": [{"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_02_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/issues/02-pr-split-reuse-and-assignment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_02_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_split_reuse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/issues/02-pr-split-reuse-and-assignment.md", "source_location": null, "weigh